#! ia 1.0

@capability schema-method
  meaning
    says "Work with schema records under the IA methodology: the schema-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a schema. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a schema?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook schema-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook schema-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with schema records, each the structural contract of exactly one registered word: orient through ia position --word schema and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with schema records?"
  subject
    subject-word schema
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word schema at the seat the work concerns, read the schema records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary schema --schema for the sections and fields a schema carries."
      Inference means "Read the word's schema with ia vocabulary <word> --schema: its sections, required fields and edges."
      Decision means "schema is a floor word that every workspace admits; seat the work at the system that owns the records it touches."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these schema records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the schema must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Fit the records to the schema; a change to a schema belongs to the system that owns its word."
      Decision means "Extend an existing schema through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the schema will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the schema; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Fill each record's required sections and fields from the schema, and propose a schema change to its owner rather than authoring around it."
      Decision means "Use schemas, never author one here: a new schema registers a word, which is authoring a system and lies outside this kit (by hand from the public IA documentation, or with an InventArch subscription)."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Run ia validate; a schema finding names the section or field to fix."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the schema, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."

@capability system-method
  meaning
    says "Work with system records under the IA methodology: the system-method playbook's orient, plan, act and learn cells for finding, planning, changing and checking a system. It grants no authority; the workspace's mandates decide what the participant may change."
    answers "Which procedure does an agent follow for a system?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook system-method]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@playbook system-method
  meaning
    says "How an agent works with system records, each a registration of vocabulary, direct system dependencies, a local steward and consent for relationships: orient through ia position --word system and the word's schema, plan through the owner of the word, change records only through ia preview, ia author and ia validate, and leave the account reconciled."
    answers "How does an agent work with system records?"
  subject
    subject-word system
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Run ia position --word system at the seat the work concerns, read the system records it points at with ia read, and run ia vocabulary system --schema for the sections and fields a system carries."
      Inference means "Read the systems the workspace composes, the words each owns and its steward, with ia position --seat <system>."
      Decision means "system is a floor word that every workspace admits; seat the work at the system that owns the records it touches."
      Learning means "Read the observations and improvements earlier work left on these system records before repeating it."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the system must satisfy: the intent, the blocking rules and the mandate at the seat, and the ceiling of any provisional foundation."
      Inference means "Decide which system owns each word the work needs, and seat the work there."
      Decision means "Extend an existing system through its owner where one covers the need, and bring each consequential choice to the person with a recommendation."
      Learning means "Say how the system will be judged and what would leave it inconclusive."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Read what ia preview compiles for the system; a refusal means the plan is wrong about the record, not that the check is in the way."
      Inference means "Use the system: author records of its words at its seat, through its steward, as those words' own playbooks say."
      Decision means "Use, read and seat at systems; authoring a new system or extending a system's vocabulary lies outside this kit (by hand from the public IA documentation, or with an InventArch subscription)."
      Learning means "Keep each refusal with its code, fix it within the step, and preview again."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run ia validate and the checks that apply, report them verbatim, and say which claims they evidence and which stay unevaluated."
      Inference means "Check that each record sits in the system that owns its word, and that the system's requires still cover what it uses."
      Decision means "Reconcile the records that cite or depend on the system, and leave the handoff packet method-handoff-packet describes."
      Learning means "Propose what the work taught to the owners concerned, as method-improvement-lifecycle describes, or state that there is none."
